:"Imiesłów perfectum czasownika deponentnego „morior”. Z domyślnym „est” (w021) znaczy „umarł”.","w036":"Współdzieli domyślne „est” (w021)."},"en":{"w029":"A deponent participle with active meaning, sharing the understood “est” (w021).","w032":"The second part of the name “Póntio Piláto”.","w033":"Shares the understood “est” (w021).","w034":"The perfect participle of the deponent “morior”. With understood “est” (w021), it means “died”.","w036":"Shares the understood “est” (w021)."}}},{"id":"s05","type":"verse","w":[{"i":"w037","f":"descéndit","l":"descendo","m":186},{"i":"w038","f":"ad","l":"ad","m":3,"h":"w039"},{"i":"w039","f":"ínferos","l":"inferi","p":";","m":90}],"tr":{"pl":"zstąpił do piekieł,","en":"He descended into hell;"},"tc":{"pl":[114],"en":[115,116]},"g":{"pl":["zstąpił","do","otchłani"],"en":["descended","to","the realm of the dead"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w039":"Rzeczownik w liczbie mnogiej po „ad”. Oznacza tych, którzy są niżej, lub ich krainę."},"en":{"w039":"A plural noun after “ad”, denoting those below or their realm."}}},{"id":"s06","type":"verse","w":[{"i":"w040","f":"tértia","l":"tertius","m":31,"h":"w041"},{"i":"w041","f":"die","l":"dies","m":210},{"i":"w042","f":"resurréxit","l":"resurgo","m":186},{"i":"w043","f":"a","l":"ab","m":0,"h":"w044"},{"i":"w044","f":"mórtuis","l":"mortuus","p":";","m":196,"s":true}],"tr":{"pl":"trzeciego dnia zmartwychwstał,","en":"the third day He rose again from the dead;"},"tc":{"pl":[114],"en":[115,116]},"g":{"pl":["trzeciego","dnia","zmartwychwstał","spośród","umarłych"],"en":["on the third","day","rose again","from","the dead"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w041":"Ablativus czasu. Tutaj rodzaj żeński, który zgadza się z „tértia” (w040)."},"en":{"w041":"Ablative of time. Feminine here, agreeing with “tértia” (w040)."}}},{"id":"s07","type":"verse","w":[{"i":"w045","f":"ascéndit","l":"ascendo","m":186},{"i":"w046","f":"ad","l":"ad","m":3,"h":"w047"},{"i":"w047","f":"cælos","l":"caelum","p":";","m":90,"a":3}],"tr":{"pl":"wstąpił na nieb